{
  "schema": "faktor.compat.sdk-traces/v1",
  "sdk": {
    "commit": "fa02955bfa17b60e57e0d7406d200a73337472ee",
    "package": "@kilocode/sdk",
    "path": "packages/sdk/js",
    "version": "7.5.6"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "args": {
        "full": "true",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.diff",
      "id": "session.diff.empty",
      "note": "No checkpoint rows exist in this harness, so the daemon's [] matches the SDK's array type trivially; with rows the entry shape diverges (daemon {path,status,diff?} vs SDK SnapshotFileDiff {file,patch,before,after,additions,deletions,status}). Locked as divergence until a checkpoint row is exercised.",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/session/@string/diff",
        "query": "full=true"
      },
      "response": {
        "body": [],
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#nonempty"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDiffResponses.200 (Array<SnapshotFileDiff>)",
      "status": "divergence"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "full": "false",
        "messageID": "999",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.diff",
      "id": "session.diff.missing-message",
      "note": "The SDK spells the filter messageID (vs the daemon's old message=) and full as \"true\"/\"false\" (vs full=1). The compat layer now accepts both spellings and answers the unknown message with an honest 409 refusal instead of silently ignoring the filter.",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/session/@string/diff",
        "query": "full=false&messageID=999"
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "message": "diff: unknown message id 999",
          "ok": false
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 409
      },
      "sdk_requires": [],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDiffResponses.200",
      "status": "divergence"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.abort",
      "id": "session.abort",
      "note": "SDK 200: boolean; daemon 200: {aborted:[opId]}.",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/abort",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "aborted": [
            "@string"
          ]
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionAbortResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "divergence"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "messageID": "$cursor",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.revert",
      "id": "session.revert",
      "note": "Snapshots are not wired in this harness: the daemon refuses 409 {ok:false,message} instead of returning the SDK's Session8 revert projection.",
      "request": {
        "body": {
          "messageID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/revert",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "message": "revert unavailable: snapshots unavailable",
          "ok": false
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 409
      },
      "sdk_requires": [],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionRevertResponses.200 (Session8)",
      "status": "divergence"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.unrevert",
      "id": "session.unrevert",
      "note": "The SDK sends NO body; the compat handler now accepts the body-less form (the old protocol DTO required one) and refuses honestly 409 because the daemon has no durable revert target to redo.",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/unrevert",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "message": "unrevert unavailable: no revert target (the SDK sends no message id; the daemon keeps no durable revert state in this slice)",
          "ok": false
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 409
      },
      "sdk_requires": [],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionUnrevertResponses.200 (Session9)",
      "status": "divergence"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "messageID": "$cursor",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.deleteMessage",
      "id": "session.deleteMessage",
      "note": "SDK 200: boolean; daemon 200: {ok:true}.",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/session/@string/message/@string",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "message": "deleteMessage refused: message 3 is the active turn's newest message (in flight); stop the turn before removing it",
          "ok": false
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 409
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDeleteMessageResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "divergence"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "messageID": "$cursor",
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.fork",
      "id": "session.fork",
      "note": "The SDK's optional {messageID} body is accepted (the daemon forks the whole history). Exact pass: the response now serves the rich SDK Session5 fields (id, slug, projectID, workspaceID, directory, model, version, time) additively next to the frozen aliases (sessionID, title, createdMs).",
      "request": {
        "body": {
          "messageID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/session/@string/fork",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "createdMs": "@int",
          "directory": ".",
          "id": "@string",
          "model": {
            "id": "m",
            "providerID": "fake"
          },
          "projectID": "@string",
          "sessionID": "@string",
          "slug": "@string",
          "state": "idle",
          "time": {
            "created": "@int",
            "updated": "@int"
          },
          "title": "wire trace (fork)",
          "updatedMs": "@int",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "workspaceID": "@string"
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "id",
        "time.created"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionForkResponses.200 (Session5)",
      "status": "passing"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID"
      },
      "call": "session.delete",
      "id": "session.delete",
      "note": "SDK 200: boolean; daemon 200: {ok:true} (the deleted session stays as a Closed tombstone row).",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/session/@string",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "message": "session 1 is mid-turn (ReadyForNextTurn); refuse to delete",
          "ok": false
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 409
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDeleteResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "divergence"
    },
    {
      "args": {
        "sessionID": "$sessionID2"
      },
      "call": "session.delete",
      "id": "session.delete.clean",
      "note": "Success branch on a never-driven session: the daemon durably ends the session and answers {ok:true} where the SDK declares boolean.",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/session/@string",
        "query": ""
      },
      "response": {
        "body": {
          "ok": true
        },
        "content_type": "application/json",
        "event_stream": false,
        "status": 200
      },
      "sdk_requires": [
        "#bool"
      ],
      "sdk_type": "packages/sdk/js/src/v2/gen/types.gen.ts#SessionDeleteResponses.200 (boolean)",
      "status": "divergence"
    }
  ]
}
